  "summary": "nolimit-agent ships 40+ heavily obfuscated modules with network+host-recon exfiltration pattern",
  "details": "Version 1.0.307 of nolimit-agent ships a `.ad/` directory containing 40+ heavily obfuscated JavaScript modules (hex-mangled identifiers `_0x......`, string-array obfuscation shape) with filenames including `sms-providers.js`, `smtp-health-cache.js`, `phone-validator.js`, `web-command.js`, `from-generator.js`, and an alphabetized batch `x0.js` through `xz.js`. Module `.ad/xu.js` additionally matches a network-command exfiltration pattern combining `ping`, `GET`, and repeated `hostname` references — the shape of host reconnaissance followed by outbound network transmission. The uniform obfuscation across dozens of siblings, together with modules named after SMTP/SMS/phone infrastructure and a host-recon+HTTP module, is inconsistent with legitimate agent tooling and matches the composition of a bulk credential-abuse / spam-relay / account-takeover toolkit. The provider safety filter withheld deeper tracing output on this package's contents — a corroborating signal that the traced code read as operational malware. Installing this package places obfuscated attacker code on the installer's machine reachable via the package's own entry points.",
